WEBVTT

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:13.860
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:14.070
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:37.030
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:43.040
<b>Chapter Seven                 Gray Boundary</b>

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.960
The encyclopedias and literature collections 
were there from the start.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:52.350
You mean from when she first 
went into to that room?

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:53.210
Yes.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.460
"Everything becomes F"... Fifteen...

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.470
Each set only went to volume 15.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.120
Any idea why?

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:04.650
No...

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:08.230
All we do is buy what she asks.

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:12.110
She bought a lot of stuff.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:13.710
Those blocks, for example.

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:16.000
We didn't even know what some of the stuff was.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.990
<b>Food 
Blocks 
Clothes 
Food 
TV Parts 
Microwave 
Food 
Food 
Food 
General Supplies</b>

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:17.990
TV parts?

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.920
You saw that old TV in her room?

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:24.120
Something in it broke, so we got her those.

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:26.640
That was last April.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:28.910
She repaired it herself?

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:30.420
I'm sure.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:33.010
But it's so old...

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.480
Wouldn't it have been cheaper to just buy a new one?

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:37.240
I thought the same thing,

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:40.210
but maybe she liked it.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:43.520
She spent fifteen years in that room.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:45.310
Who was here,

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:49.590
in the lab, during the incident fifteen years ago?

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:52.410
Let's see... Me?

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:55.320
And Mizutani, the programmer...

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:57.270
And the director's wife.

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.900
Where's Mizutani-san's room?

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.110
Did you learn anything?

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:09.160
No, nothing really.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.520
Want to play some, to get your mind off it?

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:14.340
You, too, if you'd like, Sensei.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.730
This place may seem a bit sterile,

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.690
but it does have something like 
an entertainment facility.

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:21.790
Sorry,

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:24.750
but we have to solve the case 
before the police arrive.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:25.480
Go.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:26.370
Sensei?

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:28.970
I'd like to be able to keep thinking 
about things, so I'll pass.

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:32.010
But at this rate, you'll turn into 
an octopus rice cracker.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:33.570
Hey, Sensei!

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:36.260
An octopus rice cracker?

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:38.280
It's a meaningless joke.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:42.810
Too bad...

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:46.410
I'd met with the doctor

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:49.820
several times before the incident.

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:52.190
She was fourteen, right?

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:53.950
She was so pretty...

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.040
She'd just come back from America,

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:59.460
and everyone was saying what a genius she was.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:02.080
The press was here a lot.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:05.860
But since the incident, no one had seen her.

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:08.730
Not as far as I know.

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:11.730
What do you think the killer was after?

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:15.740
How the hell would I know?

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:20.220
For example, was there some data 
that would be worth killing over?

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:24.200
Well, we are talking about Magata Shiki.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.070
There may have been something

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:28.890
worth billions of yen, maybe more.

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:31.350
But I don't know if it'd be worth a life.

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:34.350
Did anyone have a grudge against the director?

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:38.500
At some point, you started acting 
like a detective, didn't you?

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:42.060
I'm just a plain, old university lecturer.

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:46.140
No one had a grudge against him.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:49.040
As a researcher, you should understand them.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:51.480
This is the best possible environment.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:54.470
I can't see anyone being upset over anything.

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:56.890
Then the killer came from outside?

00:04:56.890 --> 00:05:01.220
No, it's impossible for someone 
to enter from the outside.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:04.490
There are no secret ways in or out of the facility.

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:07.370
Whoever did this just doesn't feel human, you know?

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:12.870
Oh, Saikawa-sensei.

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:16.190
I couldn't find Miki-san's bag.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.760
The killer probably stole it...

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:22.880
There was a present for the doctor inside, right?

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:24.900
So I've heard.

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:28.560
But there may have been something 
else important inside.

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:30.470
Did you ask Miki-san?

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:32.890
No, I'll do that now.

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:34.860
Ah, Yamane-san?

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:38.360
Hey, how old are you, Nishinosono-san?

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:39.810
Almost twenty.

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:41.360
When is your birthday?

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:42.670
December.

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:45.210
You still have four months to go!

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:47.600
You can't wait to be an adult, can you?

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:52.640
You have such pretty hands...

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:54.470
You've never really suffered in your life.

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:56.070
That isn't—

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:57.630
Left-handed, huh?

00:05:57.630 --> 00:05:59.460
No ring, of course.

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:02.820
Shimada-san, are you single?

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:05.860
Yeah, no interest in men at all.

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:07.910
I'd rather watch anime.

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:09.460
I understand...

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:12.760
But Saikawa-sensei's great, isn't he?

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:15.910
But you just said you weren't interested in guys.

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:19.140
Because he doesn't seem to be alive.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:22.230
Like his heart isn't beating at all.

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:24.400
It makes me feel giddy.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:25.860
Do you understand?

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:26.860
No.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:29.650
I'm sure you don't. You're still nineteen.

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:32.280
He may look cold,

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:34.180
but Sensei is actually really nice.

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:36.010
Can you give me an example?

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:37.180
Well...

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:40.800
I can't think of one right now.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:45.130
You're so warm.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:47.210
You're cute, Nishinosono-san!

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.910
But I don't think

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.290
you have a chance.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:55.520
Excuse me.

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:56.690
Come in.

00:06:58.110 --> 00:06:59.490
Saikawa Sohei.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.780
You must be Professor Saikawa.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:10.360
Mr. Yamane told me you would be coming.

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:13.850
Um, I need to get going...

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:17.400
Hey, Nishinosono-san?

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:17.830
Yes?

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:20.260
Want to do something fun?

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:22.120
F-Fun?

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:23.150
That.

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:25.750
Come on, undress.

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:28.210
Are you alone?

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:31.060
I heard that there was a female helping you

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:32.780
with the investigation.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:36.640
One of the workers here took 
her to the recreation room.

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:38.470
Oh, really?

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:49.030
2-B 
Shimada

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:46.540
Um, I didn't really understand what you just said.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:51.410
Well, once you're in this, you can see 
whatever your brain imagines.

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:53.070
That's just silly.

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:55.670
Here we go. You ready?

00:07:56.550 --> 00:07:59.040
H-Hey, wait...

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.660
Who would make a toy this dangerous?

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.160
Dr. Magata Shiki.

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:09.460
It's pitch-black! Shimada-san!

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:10.920
Here you go.

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:12.220
Thank you.

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:15.870
I know this isn't the time to ask you about this.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:17.630
It's fine.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:20.850
I do hope it doesn't take too much time, though.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:23.330
It shouldn't be too long.

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:25.080
I have three questions.

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:29.470
First, did you notice anything different

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:32.160
with Mr. Shindo when you were together?

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:34.250
Not particularly.

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:38.360
Do you have any idea who may be responsible

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:41.910
for the murders of Dr. Magata and Mr. Shindo?

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:43.120
Not at all.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:45.400
Do you know why anyone

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:47.710
would want to murder Dr. Magata?

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:50.000
I really don't know.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:51.810
I see.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:54.970
It shouldn't come as a surprise.

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:57.880
I barely know anything about my sister.

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:00.510
Due to our family's situation,

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:03.100
we've been separated since I was born.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:08.010
And after the incident fifteen years ago, 
we grew even further apart.

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:09.770
Is that so?

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:15.490
It's a journal.

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:18.070
I write in it every day.

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:21.160
You know, to make sure I don't forget everything.

00:09:26.510 --> 00:09:29.170
What kind of person was Shiki?

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:32.750
My apologies.

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:36.440
If you don't feel like answering, I understand.

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:39.680
Are you interested in my sister?

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:40.680
Yes.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:44.060
In addition to learning about her accomplishments,

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:49.710
I've also read up on as much of her literature 
and interviews as possible,

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:54.690
and I was incredibly impressed by 
her unique, amazing intellect.

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:58.590
I truly wish I could have had the opportunity

00:09:58.590 --> 00:10:00.410
to speak with her directly.

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:04.840
I'm sure my sister would have 
loved talking with you.

00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:06.790
I don't know about that.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:11.110
Through all of my research, 
she never seemed like someone

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:13.310
who could be easily entertained.

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:14.940
I see...

00:10:16.430 --> 00:10:19.550
I've actually only met her a few times.

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:24.680
She lived in America during her 
elementary and middle school years.

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:27.520
Even so, every time we met,

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:30.330
it was an eye-opening experience.

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:33.960
I mean, from her personality to the way she thinks,

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:37.070
everything was just so different from me.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.820
It's hard to explain.

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:43.990
She had this power to just draw me in.

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:47.590
It felt as if we were like the same person.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:50.330
Does that make any sense?

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:51.890
Yes,

00:10:51.890 --> 00:10:54.840
although I never had the chance 
to meet your sister.

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:57.090
Oh, that's right.

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:58.490
Actually,

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:00.590
we have met.

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:04.080
But it was after she was no longer with us.

00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:08.100
She looked so much younger than her actual age.

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:11.170
It's because time had stopped for her.

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:15.250
Fifteen years in a place like this...

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:18.110
I can't even imagine.

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:21.360
But... I hope this doesn't come off wrong...

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:25.930
I truly believe she felt happy with her life here.

00:11:25.930 --> 00:11:28.750
Yes, I completely agree!

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:31.160
I can't speak directly for her,

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:35.160
but I think this is, ultimately, what she wanted.

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:39.810
Do you mind if I ask a question?

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:40.720
Feel free.

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:45.850
Women aren't really your strong suit, are they?

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:49.270
I can't say that they are.

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:51.770
You also look like you are actually

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:54.010
a very emotional person,

00:11:54.010 --> 00:11:57.020
but choose to hold those emotions back.

00:11:57.370 --> 00:11:59.210
You are quite perceptive.

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:02.530
You and my sister seem to have

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:04.970
some similar characteristics.

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:08.540
I'm honored you would think that.

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:11.370
Professor, why do you want to know about

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:13.360
what happened to my sister?

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:17.920
Well, I feel it's my imperative to find out.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:20.050
For your sake? Or...

00:12:20.390 --> 00:12:21.550
I don't know.

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:26.280
Oh, I almost forgot.

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:29.930
It seems they couldn't find your 
bag in the helicopter.

00:12:30.690 --> 00:12:32.180
Is that so?

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:36.300
It was a present for your sister, correct?

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:38.940
Yes. A doll.

00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:40.480
A doll?

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:43.340
Is something wrong?

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:46.700
It's just a presumption.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:50.190
I think the only thing that really interested

00:12:50.190 --> 00:12:52.660
your sister was the human mind.

00:12:53.610 --> 00:12:56.960
So, to her, I believe a human body

00:12:56.960 --> 00:13:00.960
and a doll were, more or less, the same thing.

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:02.680
You know what?

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:06.590
A memory I have of my sister just came to me.

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:08.470
I'd love to hear it.

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:13.790
It was after I fell off a swing

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:16.230
and scratched my knee on the ground.

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:19.840
Once I saw the blood, I started to cry.

00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:21.860
And my sister said,

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:26.310
"The human body is nothing but a simple container."

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:30.990
She then put her hand on my cheek and said,

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:36.510
"That's why, no matter how damaged 
your physical body may get,

00:13:36.510 --> 00:13:40.110
my feelings for you will never change."

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:47.160
Why did everything have to turn out this way?

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:52.030
Humans are truly foolish creatures!

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:57.170
Oh, how I wish I could escape this unjust world!

00:13:58.380 --> 00:13:59.840
I feel the same.

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:06.560
No, I can't say things like that.

00:14:06.870 --> 00:14:09.030
My sister would laugh at me.

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:12.650
This might not be the time or place to say this,

00:14:12.650 --> 00:14:15.030
but I enjoyed talking with you.

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:16.630
As did I.

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:20.620
I have a feeling we will meet again someday.

00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:31.760
No way!

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:33.890
What? What? What do you see?

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:35.010
It's a secret!

00:15:02.530 --> 00:15:05.810
You're capable of laughing so innocently, Sensei?

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:08.880
Oh, Saikawa-sensei, right?

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:10.970
I just did something naughty with him.

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:11.970
Shimada-san!

00:15:13.650 --> 00:15:15.970
You're capable of being so excited?

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:29.290
Did you call me?

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:39.310
Who are you?

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:42.710
I've heard that question before.

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:46.340
I am Michiru.

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:48.420
Stop joking around!

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:00.930
Who's playing this trick on me?

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:02.890
And using Dr. Magata's data...

00:16:03.340 --> 00:16:04.350
Shimada-san?

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:07.860
No. I am Michiru.

00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:10.940
Where are you? Let's meet in person.

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:13.400
I'm right in front of you.

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:15.620
I meant in the real world!

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:18.310
To me, this is reality.

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:21.510
You called me.

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:23.460
What do you mean?

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:25.580
Nishinosono-san,

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:27.820
you lost your parents, did you not?

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:30.900
Do you remember that day?

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:35.050
Wasn't it night when the accident happened?

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.030
Why?

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:45.560
Did you cry?

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:50.870
I survived...

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:54.000
I was the only one to survive.

00:16:55.870 --> 00:16:57.770
I am the same.

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:06.580
What were you wearing that night?

00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:08.640
Purple.

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:10.660
That night,

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:13.690
I was wearing a purple dress.

00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:20.400
I loved it. My mother made it for me...

00:17:20.860 --> 00:17:23.070
What happened to it?

00:17:23.370 --> 00:17:24.650
I threw it away.

00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:25.660
Why?

00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:28.010
Because it got stained.

00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:29.750
How did it get stained?

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:31.510
Blood...

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:34.250
It got stained with blood.

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:37.650
I washed it so many times.

00:17:38.110 --> 00:17:41.530
Even though I'd never done 
any cleaning in my life.

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:46.260
I washed it, but the blood wouldn't come out.

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:49.750
So I got sad and threw it out.

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:51.960
Whose blood was it?

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:53.380
I don't know.

00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:55.060
Nishinosono-san,

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:57.260
I want to ask you a question.

00:17:58.290 --> 00:18:01.860
You lost the people you cared for.

00:18:01.860 --> 00:18:04.330
So how were you able to survive?

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:06.110
I don't know the answer to that!

00:18:06.110 --> 00:18:09.170
Were you really alone?

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:14.330
When it happened, I'm certain there 
was someone next to you.

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:18.330
Sensei...

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:40.860
Saikawa-sensei...

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:43.990
Nishinosono-san, in this place,

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:47.480
you can see the things you 
want to know right away.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:50.270
The people you want to talk to 
are always in front of you.

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:53.420
The original world was like this.

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:56.940
The world you live in is a very restrictive place.

00:18:57.300 --> 00:18:59.750
Even if you are given a lot of information,

00:19:00.050 --> 00:19:03.880
it is all quickly forgotten and lost.

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:07.080
But it isn't really supposed to be that way.

00:19:08.090 --> 00:19:11.190
Nishinosono-san, will you come to this side?

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:16.840
What's wrong? It isn't scary.

00:19:17.730 --> 00:19:20.270
This is how the world was supposed to be.

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:24.860
Too bad.

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:27.600
Farewell. I hope we can meet again.

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:32.350
Nishinosono-san! Nishinosono-san!

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:34.380
Nishinosono-san!

00:19:36.850 --> 00:19:38.240
Thank goodness...

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:40.760
What were you seeing?

00:19:41.970 --> 00:19:44.580
Something very important.

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:50.580
Excuse me.

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:51.760
Sensei!

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:53.830
Put some clothes on, Nishinosono-kun.

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:55.270
I saw her!

00:19:55.900 --> 00:19:56.710
Saw whom?

00:19:56.710 --> 00:19:57.920
Dr. Magata.

00:20:01.850 --> 00:20:04.490
Good evening, Aunt Yumiko.

00:20:05.590 --> 00:20:08.810
But it looks like you're a little late.

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:30.200
Uncle,

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:33.860
I got your birthday present dirty.

00:20:34.470 --> 00:20:35.420
Yeah.

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:39.680
Can I live on my own, as long as I have this?

00:20:40.010 --> 00:20:40.700
Yeah.

00:20:41.820 --> 00:20:43.850
I did everything myself,

00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:46.680
and you tried to stop me.

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:48.340
Do you understand?

00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:51.930
Shiki, please kill me.

00:20:52.630 --> 00:20:54.490
It's okay, Uncle.

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:57.560
I'm certain we'll be killed someday.

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:02.300
Until that happens,

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:06.070
let us live righteously, believing in human pride.

00:21:07.890 --> 00:21:09.730
<i>I have never forgotten</i>

00:21:10.210 --> 00:21:12.330
<i>those words.</i>
